---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How v0id.me is built: Astro on Cloudflare Workers, no JavaScript for readers, and a status signed on my Mac.">
  <div class="tree-page">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>

    <p class="section-label">the site</p>
    <ul class="tree-links section-list">
      <li>Astro on Cloudflare Workers. Every page is plain HTML and CSS; no JavaScript is sent to readers.</li>
      <li>Verdana, small text, gray buttons, laid out after paulgraham.com.</li>
      <li>Posts are markdown files, edited directly or through Sveltia CMS. The source is <a href="https://github.com/v0id-user/peace-land">on GitHub</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="section-label">the sidebar</p>
    <ul class="tree-links section-list">
      <li>The Spotify block and the status under it are a small page the sidebar reloads every 15 seconds. The Worker asks Spotify for what is playing; nothing runs in your browser.</li>
      <li>The status comes from a reporter on my Mac. It reads the lid, whether I am at the keyboard, and my Claude Code sessions, and sends only what changed. Before the Mac sleeps it says so.</li>
      <li>Every report is signed with <a href="/pgp/">my OpenPGP key</a>. The Worker holds only the public key and drops anything it cannot verify, and anyone can check the last report with <code>curl -sL v0id.me/status.asc | gpg -d</code>.</li>
      <li>The git row shows my newest commit in a public repo. Private repos are filtered out before any commit is looked at.</li>
      <li>The tab icon fades to gray when I am away and pale when the laptop sleeps.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="section-label">from a terminal</p>
    <ul class="tree-links section-list">
      <li><code>curl -L v0id.me</code> answers in plain text, my key is found with <code>gpg --locate-keys hey@v0id.me</code>, and the <a href="/guestbook/">guestbook</a> can be signed with curl. The full list is under <a href="/misc/">misc</a>.</li>
      <li>Guestbook entries wait for me to approve them with a command signed by the same key.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
